Vlad Dogaru wrote:
>
> hit me with the
> full explanations. What is the difference between MR and reflection and
> how do you get each one?

Reflection will cause any "ray" class wand zap to bounce off you.
The equivalent spells and other sources of rays bounce also.
One fun strategy is to zap straight at a monster where it's you,
the monster, a wall.  The ray will hit the monster, bounce off the
wall, hist the monster, bounce off you, hit the monster, and so
on until it runs out of range.  Compare with beam zaps that don't
bounce and aren't effected by reflection.

Magic resistance gives immunity to a specific list of dangers
only a couple of which are "ray" class.  For a full write-up on
MR see the spoiler for dragon colors:

http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/343/drgn-343.html

There is some amount of overlap - Magic missiles in particular
stop being a problem with either.  It's the non-overlapping items
that make both important.



